 ],
 "note": "Appendix §H, Recovery rule 2. c1 executes P1 with P2 queued; the runtime crashes (no clean close). At the restart P2 is durably rejected (authorization history unknown) before anything is dispatched, although its principal reconnects with control at once and no revocation happened: without a clean close the host can't establish that none did. P1, executing, is outcome_unknown as before. The cost: the same id returns the rejected receipt and is never re-admitted; the client sends the prompt again with a new request_id, which is admitted and acquires."
}
